                              NewQoute v1.0.
                              --------------

 NewQuote is a replacement for the old RandQuote-program for CNet.
 It's slightly faster than the old one, and have no limits about
 the length of the quotes. I.E It could be anything from 1 to 1000 lines
 if you wan't.

 To install NewQuote just add the following line to your sys.welcome
 file in SYSTEXT:

   #0 Pfiles:NewQuot.REXX}
   ^
   |
  This is a <CTRL+Q>

 and place your quote.txt in SYSDATA:

 The quotefile should look like this :

  21   /* Number of quotes */
  *    /* The quotes start's here*/
  Some bull..... /* The actual quote */
  *    /*Here's the end of the 1st quote*/

 and so on....

 The quote can be almost as long as you wan't, just remember to start and
 stop with a '*'. You don't have to bother about the centering of the
 quote, the program handles that too....


